From 5fa92d9eab21ae69f0f9d310a473bbba65c63563 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: caoanhhao <caoanhhao2@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 23:47:51 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 106/107] drm/msm/dsi/phy: 7nm: give the bonded slave PHY the
 master's dividers

In bonded mode the slave PHY runs from the master's PLL, but its
CMN_CLK_CFG0 dividers are its own and no clock in the tree sets them: they
keep the reset value (0xf1 on SM8250), while the master is programmed to
0x11. With the Galaxy Tab S7 LTE's dual C-PHY panel this leaves the second
link unusable: the DSI1 half stays dark and the panel stops taking the DSI0
half after ~160 lines.

The downstream driver writes the master's CLK_CFG0 to the slave before it
enables the PLL. Do the same in vco_prepare, before the PLL bias comes up.

caoanhhao used AI to code
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy_7nm.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy_7nm.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy_7nm.c
index 5decaa246..4a7c6f60e 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy_7nm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy_7nm.c
@@ -516,6 +516,15 @@ static int dsi_pll_7nm_vco_prepare(struct clk_hw *hw)
 	struct dsi_pll_7nm *pll_7nm = to_pll_7nm(hw);
 	int rc;
 
+	/*
+	 * The bonded slave PHY runs from the master's PLL but has its own
+	 * dividers, which no clock in the tree sets: copy the master's before
+	 * the PLL bias comes up.
+	 */
+	if (pll_7nm->slave)
+		dsi_pll_cmn_clk_cfg0_write(pll_7nm->slave,
+					   readl(pll_7nm->phy->base + REG_DSI_7nm_PHY_CMN_CLK_CFG0));
+
 	dsi_pll_enable_pll_bias(pll_7nm);
 	if (pll_7nm->slave)
 		dsi_pll_enable_pll_bias(pll_7nm->slave);
